# Board

The project board is the source for Estimate, Actual, Remaining Work, Waiting and Phase. Sprints are milestones;
do not add an iteration field as well.

## One-time setup

1. Create a GitHub project (org or user) and link this repo to it.
2. Add the fields: `scripts/board/bootstrap-project.sh <owner> <project-number>`.
3. In the project's **Workflows** settings, enable: *Auto-add to project* (this repo, `is:issue,pr`),
   *Item added to project* → Todo, *Item closed* → Done, *Pull request merged* → Done, *Auto-add sub-issues*.
   GitHub has no API for these, so this step is manual.
4. Run the `labels` workflow once (Actions → labels → Run workflow).

When an issue closes, its assignee sets Remaining Work to 0, records Actual, and records Waiting separately as
decision latency.

## What runs

The `labels` workflow creates or updates the labels in `.github/labels.tsv` when that file changes on `main`, or when
it is run by hand.

## Symptoms

| Symptom | Fix |
|---|---|
| An issue is missing from the board | The project's auto-add workflow is off or filtered; enable it (step 3) and add the issue |
| Labels missing on new issues | Run the `labels` workflow |
| Old issues still carry `type:question` after a template update, so they have no kind | Renaming fails, because the repo already has a `question` label. Add `question` to each one, then delete the old label: `gh issue list --label type:question --state all --json number --jq '.[].number' \| xargs -I{} gh issue edit {} --add-label question` and `gh label delete type:question --yes` |
